<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:SemanticRequirement> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "infrastructure-model-join" <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Establish UIF, the Universal Infrastructure counterpart that should own staging and production. It does not exist yet. TID in maldous/tid-semantics is the mining source for it and is not a substitute for it, so the blocker is an absent counterpart rather than an unperformed import." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:anqr:predicate:requiresDeliveryContract> <urn:usf:delivery-contract:deploymentmechanism> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:anqr:predicate:boundResourceKind> "allowed shape: a joined semantic source set, selected by a manifest, declaring the staging and production infrastructure it owns. Not a value and not a vendor choice." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:anqr:predicate:bindsEnvironment> <urn:usf:environment:staging> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:anqr:predicate:bindsEnvironment> <urn:usf:environment:productionlive> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:anqr:predicate:requiresExternalAuthority> <urn:usf:approval-authority:operator> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:anqr:predicate:unlocksEvidence> "Every other staging and production decision becomes answerable against a model rather than invented. Until the join exists, the eleven account-shaped decisions are not the blocker; they are what the blocker will ask for." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:anqr:predicate:isSecretValue> "false" <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:usf:predicate:notRequiredReason> "This repository must not author the staging or production infrastructure model. Doing so would create a second, competing model of the same thing, and the joined one would then have to be reconciled against work that had no authority to exist." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-deployment-decision-record:1> <urn:usf:predicate:member> "infrastructure-model-join" <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-deployment-decision-record:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "The staging and production infrastructure is not modelled here and is not missing by oversight. The operator states it lives in the latest tid-semantics repository, which is not present on this machine and has not been joined. The eleven decisions below are the values that model will need; they are not a substitute for it." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:SemanticModel> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "uif" <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:usf:predicate:title> "UIF, Universal Infrastructure" <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:anqr:predicate:discoveredFromEvidence> "Repository maldous/tid-semantics, private, default branch main." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:anqr:predicate:discoveredFromEvidence> "A registry indexing its own ontology, taxonomy, vocabulary, statement schema, knowledge statements, conflicts, reconciliation, costings, an ISM sweep and full assessment, a TIADD model and instances, and adversarial findings." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:anqr:predicate:discoveredFromEvidence> "An ontology declared in the USF style: it defines the nouns its machine-readable artefacts instantiate and creates no instances itself." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:anqr:predicate:discoveredFromEvidence> "A v3 tree carrying semantic, sources, provenance, publication, audit, reviews, procurement and deliverable subtrees, plus a TIDv3 decision-baseline archive with a recorded digest." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:anqr:predicate:boundResourceKind> "observed head of main at discovery: 94bfb1f98ddbad18fa5e24a8800e6a9f181da8a1" <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:anqr:predicate:unresolvedDecision> "It carries no tag and no release, so a join has no released identity to bind to. Pinning must be by an operator-chosen commit, and choosing one is not this repository’s decision." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:anqr:predicate:unresolvedDecision> "It declares its own ontology. A join is a reconciliation between two vocabularies, not an import: which TID nouns correspond to USF delivery contracts and capability ports has to be decided, and deciding it wrongly would silently mis-bind every staging requirement." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:anqr:predicate:unresolvedDecision> "Whether the join is by manifest import of its sources, by a projection into USF, or by a reciprocal binding record. Each has a different blast radius and only one is right." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:anqr:predicate:requiresExternalAuthority> <urn:usf:approval-authority:operator> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Reading a public interface of a private repository establishes that it exists and what shape it has. It establishes nothing about whether its content is current, correct, or the model the operator means to join." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:anqr:predicate:requiresDeliveryContract> <urn:usf:delivery-contract:releaseprovenance> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:anqr:predicate:appliesToFacet> <urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:environment-binding:hermetic> <urn:anqr:predicate:boundResourceKind> "operator statement: Runs locally on infrastructure currently in use. Hermetic means no network and no ambient tool, not absent infrastructure." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:environment-binding:localdev> <urn:anqr:predicate:boundResourceKind> "operator statement: Runs locally on infrastructure currently in use: a developer machine serving the built output." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:environment-binding:ci> <urn:anqr:predicate:boundResourceKind> "operator statement: Runs the canonical chain on a clean checkout using the automation currently in use." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:environment-binding:integrationtest> <urn:anqr:predicate:boundResourceKind> "operator statement: Runs the composed application locally against real contracts using infrastructure currently in use." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:usf:predicate:doesNotDuplicate> "USF owns semantic authority; UIF owns infrastructure. They are counterparts rather than layers of each other, so joining UIF must not absorb its ontology into USF nor restate USF vocabulary inside UIF." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "UIF, Universal Infrastructure: the intended infrastructure counterpart to USF, Universal Service Foundation. It does not exist yet as authority. Staging and production infrastructure is therefore not modelled anywhere, and this repository must not model it in place of the counterpart that should own it." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:usf:predicate:objectiveEvidence> "Operator statement. TID, Technical Infrastructure Design, is a legacy design package of HLD and S1 to S14 schedules held in maldous/tid-semantics. Its role is a semantic-mining lens: evidence of concepts, requirements, relationships and intended behaviours worth recovering. It is not production evidence, not graph authority, and not automatically the target architecture." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:usf:predicate:doesNotDuplicate> "TID sits upstream of the lifecycle as material from which meaning is recovered, in the same position as the legacy ANQR source. Recovering meaning from it is mining; adopting it would be reproducing another project’s design as though it were an obligation." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Nothing here adopts TID content, commits to its architecture, or claims any part of it applies. Discovery established that the corpus exists and what shape it has; it established nothing about what should be recovered from it." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "UIF is a name for something not yet built. Naming it does not create it, and a blocker that names an absent counterpart is still an absent counterpart." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-resource-class:managed-free-tier> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:SemanticRequirement> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-resource-class:managed-free-tier> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "managed-free-tier" <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-resource-class:managed-free-tier> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "ANQR’s staging and production resources are managed services on free tiers: a static and function host, an edge and DNS layer, and third-party services such as error reporting and advertising. ANQR requires no physical infrastructure of any kind." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-resource-class:managed-free-tier> <urn:usf:predicate:objectiveEvidence> "Operator statement. The resource class is authorised; the accounts, sites, names and credentials within it are not, and remain the external decisions recorded separately." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-resource-class:managed-free-tier> <urn:anqr:predicate:bindsEnvironment> <urn:usf:environment:staging> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-resource-class:managed-free-tier> <urn:anqr:predicate:bindsEnvironment> <urn:usf:environment:productionlive> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-resource-class:managed-free-tier> <urn:anqr:predicate:bindsProfileRevision> <urn:anqr:profile-revision:3> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-resource-class:managed-free-tier> <urn:usf:predicate:doesNotDuplicate> "This is a resource class, not a vendor binding. Naming the class authorises the shape of the answer; the environment binding still holds the account, the site identifier and the configuration identity, and none of those are decided here." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:delivery-resource-class:managed-free-tier> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Authorising a resource class provisions nothing, deploys nothing and creates no account. It removes a question about what kind of thing staging and production are, and leaves every question about which particular things they will be." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:anqr:predicate:explicitlyNotRequired> <urn:anqr:profile-revision:3> <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-infrastructure-model:uif> <urn:usf:predicate:notRequiredReason> "ANQR does not require it. UIF concerns physical infrastructure, and ANQR runs entirely on managed services with no physical infrastructure at all. UIF remains the absent counterpart for products that do need it; ANQR is not one of them, so ANQR’s staging and production are not blocked on it." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
<urn:anqr:external-decision:infrastructure-model-join> <urn:usf:predicate:notRequiredReason> "Withdrawn as an ANQR blocker. It was recorded when the staging and production resource class was unknown; with ANQR on managed services requiring no physical infrastructure, the UIF counterpart is not on ANQR’s path. The remaining blockers are the account-shaped decisions within the authorised resource class." <urn:anqr:graph:environment-bindings> .
